 ## Overview
-This method generates a Sparse Voxel List (SVL) containing splat geometry across multiple levels of detail (LOD) by iteratively downsampling a voxel occupancy mask and extracting simplified splat primitives for each level [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard hierarchical splatting by explicitly constructing a contiguous buffer of geometry items for all LOD levels simultaneously during the meshing phase, rather than traversing a tree structure at render time to select primitives [S1, unofficial].
+This method generates a Sparse Voxel List (SVL) of splat geometry across multiple levels of detail (LOD) by iteratively downsampling a voxel occupancy mask and extracting splat primitives for each level [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently representing high-resolution voxel data for rendering by creating a hierarchy of splats, allowing the renderer to select appropriate detail levels based on screen-space footprint or error metrics. It differs from standard hierarchical splatting by explicitly constructing a flat, contiguous buffer of splat indices (`uint16_t`) organized by LOD, rather than relying solely on tree traversal during rasterization [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs**
-*   **Input:** A `ChunkSet` containing a list of `ChunkMD` structures, each representing a spatial chunk of voxel data. Each chunk contains an occupancy mask (either raw `Voxel` array or RLE compressed).
-*   **Output:** A contiguous SVL buffer (`uint16_t*`) stored in `ChunkMD.svl`, containing geometry item counts and references for each LOD level. The buffer size is determined by the total number of geometry items (`geom_items`) generated across all LODs.
+The method operates on a per-chunk basis within a larger chunk set. It assumes the input voxel data is available in a compressed (RLE) or uncompressed format and produces a geometry list suitable for GPU upload.
 
